[size=5][b]PiP Player - watch videos while you play[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]About[/b][/size]

Watch YouTube videos, livestreams, or video files from your PC in a small window in the corner of the screen while you play Skyrim or Enderal.

[list]
[*]Works in fullscreen and windowed mode, on Windows and on a Mac with CrossOver.
[*]A control panel that pauses the game while you pick a video.
[*]Pauses the video while you talk to someone, and starts it again afterwards.
[*]Picks up each video where you left off, even after you quit the game, and plays your last video again when you load a save.
[*]Change the corner, size, opacity, brightness, volume, and YouTube quality any time.
[*]Just an SKSE plugin: nothing to enable in your load order, nothing saved in your save files. You can add or remove it at any time.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url] (Enderal SE already comes with it)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download [b]PiPPlayer with YouTube[/b]. If it isn't listed under Files here, download [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer-<version>-with-YouTube.zip[/font] from [url=https://github.com/anuvgupta/skypip/releases/latest]GitHub[/url].
[*]Install it like any other mod with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex. Or, without a mod manager, extract it into your game's [font=Courier New]Data[/font] folder (the [font=Courier New]Data[/font] folder next to [font=Courier New]SkyrimSE.exe[/font]).
[*]Start the game through SKSE.
[/list]

[b]Don't want YouTube?[/b] Download [b]PiPPlayer[/b] instead. It is the same mod without the YouTube tools, so it plays only video files and direct video links.

[size=3][b]Adding YouTube later[/b][/size]

If you installed [b]PiPPlayer[/b] and change your mind, install [b]PiPPlayer YouTube Tools[/b] (under Files here, or [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer-YouTube-Tools-<version>.zip[/font] on [url=https://github.com/anuvgupta/skypip/releases/latest]GitHub[/url]). It only adds the YouTube tools.

Or get the two tools yourself and put them in [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins/PiPPlayer[/font], the folder that contains [font=Courier New]libmpv-2.dll[/font]. With Mod Organizer 2, that folder is inside the PiPPlayer mod: right-click the mod and choose Open in Explorer.

[list=1]
[*]Download [font=Courier New]yt-dlp_win.zip[/font] from [url=https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest]yt-dlp's releases[/url] and extract everything in it into that folder (you should end up with [font=Courier New]yt-dlp.exe[/font] and an [font=Courier New]_internal[/font] folder there).
[*]Download [font=Courier New]qjs-windows-x86_64.exe[/font] from [url=https://github.com/quickjs-ng/quickjs/releases/latest]QuickJS-NG's releases[/url], put it in that folder, and rename it to [font=Courier New]qjs.exe[/font].
[/list]

[size=4][b]Watch your first video[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Load a save and press [b]Left Bracket[/b]. The game pauses, a mouse cursor appears, and the control panel opens.
[*]Click the box at the top of the panel, paste a link with [b]Ctrl+V[/b], and press [b]Play[/b]. Any of these work:
[list]
[*]a YouTube link
[*]a link that ends in a video file, like [font=Courier New].mp4[/font] or [font=Courier New].webm[/font]
[*]a video file on your PC, like [font=Courier New]C:\Users\you\Videos\clip.mp4[/font]
[/list]
[*]Press [b]Left Bracket[/b] or [b]Esc[/b] to close the panel. The game unpauses and the video keeps playing in the corner.
[/list]

YouTube videos take a few seconds to start. Only public videos work: private, age-restricted, and members-only videos do not play.

[size=4][b]Keys[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Left Bracket[/b] - Open or close the control panel
[*][b]Right Bracket[/b] - Pause or resume the video
[*][b]Backslash[/b] - Show or hide the video
[/list]

These are the three keys to the right of P on a US keyboard. On other keyboard layouts, use the same three keys even if they are labeled differently. You can change them in the settings file (see below).

[size=4][b]The control panel[/b][/size]

Open it with [b]Left Bracket[/b]. Everything you change here is saved automatically.

[list]
[*][b]Play / Play clipboard[/b]: play the link in the box, or the link you last copied.
[*][b]Recent[/b]: your last 100 videos. Pick one and press [b]Resume[/b] to continue where you left off.
[*][b]Pause, Stop, Volume[/b].
[*][b]Quality[/b]: switch the playing YouTube video's quality. Lower quality is easier on your computer.
[*][b]YouTube lookup[/b]: leave it on [b]Reliable[/b]. [b]Faster[/b] starts YouTube videos about a second sooner, but a few videos may then take longer while it retries.
[*][b]Update yt-dlp[/b]: press this if YouTube videos stop playing. YouTube changes often, and an update usually fixes it.
[*][b]Conversations[/b]: the video pauses while you talk to someone and starts again 3 seconds after the conversation ends, or after a minute in which no one speaks. Change either time, or set it to off.
[*][b]Corner, Size, Opacity, Brightness, Margins[/b]: where the video sits and how it looks.
[/list]

While the panel is open, the video also has its own controls: a play/pause button, 5 second skip buttons, and a seek bar. Click the video to pause it, or drag it to another corner.

[size=4][b]Settings file[/b][/size]

Most settings are in the control panel. A few more are in [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins/PiPPlayer.ini[/font], which you can open with Notepad. Close the game before editing it.

[list]
[*][b][font=Courier New]ResumeOnStart=true[/font][/b] - Set to [font=Courier New]false[/font] to stop your last video from playing when you load a save.
[*][b][font=Courier New]Loop=false[/font][/b] - Set to [font=Courier New]true[/font] to replay a video when it ends.
[*][b][font=Courier New]CornerRadius=6[/font][/b] - How rounded the video's corners are. [font=Courier New]0[/font] makes them square.
[*][b][font=Courier New]TogglePanel[/font], [font=Courier New]TogglePause[/font], [font=Courier New]ToggleVisible[/font][/b] - The keys. Use a key name such as [font=Courier New]F8[/font], [font=Courier New]Home[/font], [font=Courier New]K[/font], or [font=Courier New]Numpad5[/font].
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Skyrim Special Edition and Anniversary Edition[/b] and [b]Enderal SE[/b]. Not for Skyrim VR or the original 2011 Skyrim.
[*][b]Mac with CrossOver:[/b] works. Videos use more CPU there; if the game slows down, pick a lower Quality. A faint click can sometimes be heard while a YouTube video is being looked up.
[*][b]SSE Display Tweaks:[/b] works.
[*][b]ENB, ReShade, Community Shaders:[/b] not tested yet; let me know how it goes.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Nothing happens when I press Left Bracket.[/b] Make sure you started the game through SKSE, and that Address Library is installed.
[*][b]A key also does something in the game.[/b] Change the key in the settings file.
[*][b]YouTube links say I need the YouTube tools.[/b] You installed the version without YouTube; see "Adding YouTube later".
[*][b]YouTube videos stopped playing.[/b] Open the panel and press [b]Update yt-dlp[/b].
[*][b]Something else.[/b] Post in the comments with the log file [font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/PiPPlayer.log[/font] attached.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]

Remove the mod in your mod manager, or delete [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer.dll[/font], [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer.ini[/font], and the [font=Courier New]PiPPlayer[/font] folder from [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins[/font]. You can do this at any time.

